lavor and aroma compound generated during fermentation, famously giving Chinese Baijiu liquor its distinctive character.","found_in":"It is found in a variety of familiar plants, including saw palmetto, bell and chili peppers, and papaya.","why_researchers_care":"Researchers are drawn to caproic acid for its dual role as a valuable product of industrial fermentation and an active metabolite in the human gut. They are particularly interested in how our microbiome converts other acids into caproic acid, and what this means for digestive and metabolic health. The strongest evidence exploring its effects in humans comes from observational studies (Oxford level 2b).","structure_function":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","statement":"Early observational work suggests caproic acid may support the body's natural defenses against certain microbes.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This is based on 4 papers, including human observational research.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":2},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}],"paper_count":4},{"claim_id":"cognition","statement":"It is being studied for a potential role in supporting focus and memory.","evidence_level":"human_observational","basis":"This rests on a single human observational study.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1}],"paper_count":1},{"claim_id":"sleep","statement":"Early animal research points toward a potential role in supporting healthy sleep and relaxation.","evidence_level":"animal","basis":"This is based on one animal study.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}],"paper_count":1},{"claim_id":"antioxidant","statement":"It may offer antioxidant properties that help protect cells from oxidative stress.","evidence_level":"animal","basis":"This rests on one animal study.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}],"paper_count":1},{"claim_id":"insect","statement":"It is being explored for its potential utility as a natural insect repellent.","evidence_level":"animal","basis":"This is based on early animal research.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}],"paper_count":1}],"hypothesized_benefits":[{"claim_id":"antimicrobial","area":"Microbiome balance","hypothesis":"Researchers are exploring whether caproic acid in the gut helps maintain a healthy microbial balance by deterring unwanted bacteria.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":4,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, placebo-controlled human trial supplementing caproic acid and measuring changes in gut microbiome composition via stool sampling over 8 weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":2},{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}]},{"claim_id":"cancer","area":"Cellular health","hypothesis":"Observational studies have detected caproic acid in the context of cellular health, leading researchers to ask if it plays a protective metabolic role in gut tissues.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":3,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized controlled trial in humans measuring markers of cellular turnover and inflammation in colon tissue biopsies after dietary supplementation with caproic acid over 12 weeks.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":3}]},{"claim_id":"sleep","area":"Sleep and relaxation","hypothesis":"If early animal findings bear out, caproic acid might interact with metabolic pathways that promote relaxation and healthy sleep cycles.","evidence_level":"animal","paper_count":1,"study_to_test_it":"A pilot human clinical trial measuring sleep latency and architecture using polysomnography in healthy adults taking a caproic acid supplement before bed for 14 days.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0007120","label":"animal model system study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"5","label":"bench or animal research"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"animal","eco":"ECO:0007120","papers":1}]},{"claim_id":"cognition","area":"Cognitive function","hypothesis":"Researchers are investigating whether circulating levels of this medium-chain fatty acid support cognitive function and memory retention.","evidence_level":"human_observational","paper_count":1,"study_to_test_it":"A randomized, double-blind human trial assessing cognitive performance using standardized memory and attention tasks before and after a 6-month caproic acid dietary intervention.","eco":{"id":"ECO:0000180","label":"clinical study evidence"},"oxford":{"level":"2b","label":"individual cohort or observational study"},"evidence_lines":[{"design":"human_observational","eco":"ECO:0000180","papers":1}]}],"associated_conditions":[{"condition":"colorectal cancer","mondo_id":"MONDO:0005575","relationship":"detected in metabolomic studies of"},{"condition":"Crohn disease","mondo_id":"MONDO:0005011","relationship":"detected in metabolomic studies of"},{"condition":"ulcerative colitis","mondo_id":"MONDO:0005101","relat